    <!-- About screen -->
    <string name="about_tagline">A surround-view dashcam for Zeekr head units: it records the 360° composite stream, with playback and a super mirror.</string>
    <string name="about_storage_title">About external storage</string>
    <string name="about_storage_body">Recordings go to external storage only, never to the head unit\'s internal flash, which cannot be replaced once worn out.\n\n• The USB drive supplied with the car is enough for basic recording.\n\n• For higher bitrates or longer retention, add a drive to the left Type-C port. It is detected automatically and can be removed at any time.\n\n• Tested: a 128 GB USB drive, and an NVMe SSD (much faster, runs slightly warmer).\n\n• Optane M10 drives are good value but small: about the last 20 hours.</string>
    <string name="about_project_title">Project</string>
    <string name="about_coffee_title">Buy the author a coffee</string>
    <string name="about_coffee_body">PayNow to 9271 6786. Optional; every feature works without it.</string>
    <string name="about_credits_title">Open source and origins</string>
    <string name="about_thanks_title">Thanks</string>
    <string name="about_thanks_body">This project grew out of an owners\' club group chat. These people gave it its start:\n\n• Jon (Zeekr 7X Singapore owners\' club) — explained how to install apps on the head unit. Nothing else would have happened without that.\n\n• SW (same club) — shared the AVM Recorder project, which showed it could be done.\n\n• Patrick (same club) — provided the key information to get started.\n\n• The Zeekr 7X Singapore owners\' club — a capable admin team and friendly members. A place where people share freely is rare.\n\n• Myself — for enthusiasm and curiosity.\n\n• Everyone using this app — I hope it makes driving a little easier.\n\n• ZEEKR and Geely — for bringing us together, and for a great car and team.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Privacy and network use</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Recordings and photos stay on your USB drive. The app does not send them anywhere.\n\n⚠ Recordings on the drive are not encrypted. Anyone with the drive can read them.\n\nThe app goes online only when you start one of these:\n\n• Check for updates: asks GitHub for the latest version. No device data is sent.\n\n• Send to phone: serves one file on your local network until you close it.\n\n• Upload logs (developer options): uploads only when you tap it.</string>
    <string name="about_project_body">Source code, issues and releases. When reporting a problem, attach a report from Diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="about_credits_evcam">Released under the GNU GPL v3.0 and based on EVCam by suyunkai, which provides the camera, recording and floating window foundations. As the GPL requires, the source code is public.</string>
    <string name="about_safety_title">Safety notice</string>
    <string name="about_safety_body">Experimental, unofficial software, not affiliated with ZEEKR. While driving, watch the road, not this app. Recordings are not guaranteed to be complete. Use at your own risk.</string>
